# ADR-0033's single ingress. No domain is configured for the local/laptop
# target (ADR-0033: "a laptop is the development and demo target only"), so
# this is `:80` rather than a domain block — Caddy only attempts automatic
# HTTPS for addresses that look like a domain name, so `:80` serves plain
# HTTP with no ACME involved.
#
# `app` is the only upstream today: no other module has a route, and there is
# no `web/` SPA yet for ADR-0052's baked-in build to serve. When one exists,
# this file gains a `handle_path` for the SPA's static assets in front of this
# reverse_proxy, matching ADR-0052's own Caddyfile.
:80 {
	log {
		output stdout
		format json
	}

	reverse_proxy app:8000
}
